  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CALEDONIA URBAN CASH ASSISTANCE PROGRAM -2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam will ensure that the wards to be targeted in Caledonia are informed by national and local level assessments that indicate the food insecurity level presenting in the district. Oxfam will also ensure that for the targeted wards, beneficiary selection process is impartial, transparent and beneficiaries are selected based on need. People with Disabilities, chronically ill (including those living with HIV&amp;AIDS), vulnerable lactating mothers, child -headed and poor female -headed households will be prioritized based on their vulnerability.  Urban Cash Assistance Programme will aim to improve and stabilize food consumption through providing cash assistance to targeted households and/or individuals, enhancing dietary diversity, and reducing negative coping strategies as well as resilience building against future shocks and stressors. The programme seeks to ensure that a greater proportion of the people assisted are women who have the responsibility of feeding their households.   The targeted population will be selected based on their increased vulnerability and limited capacities to cope with the effects of recurring droughts, epidemics and economic challenges. Women have been marginalised for a long time and have always had limited opportunities to participate in the economy making them more vulnerable than their male counterparts. People who are living with HIV and AIDS are vulnerable due to increased down time when they are sick (this compounded by poor nutrition and access to adequate food). Beneficiary registration will ensure adequate Know Your Customer (KYC) identification (i.e., Full name and surname, date of birth, place of birth and possibly beneficiary phone number).</narrative>
  </description>
